        "title": "Nano Banana 2 Lite",
        "summary": "30th June 2026 - Link Blog\n\n**[Nano Banana 2 Lite](https://deepmind.google/models/gemini-image/flash-lite/)** ([via](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48735444)) Also known as Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite",
        "content": "30th June 2026 - Link Blog\n\n**[Nano Banana 2 Lite](https://deepmind.google/models/gemini-image/flash-lite/)** ([via](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48735444)) Also known as Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite Image (`gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` [in their API](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/image-generation)), this is the \"fastest and cheapest Gemini image model, engineered for velocity and scale\".\n\nI [used AI studio](https://aistudio.google.com/app/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image) to run this prompt:\n\n> `Do a where's Waldo style image but it's where is the raccoon holding a ham radio`\n\n![](https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/nano-banana-2-lite-raccoon.jpg)\n\nI like that one better than [the results I got from the other Nano Banana models](https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/21/gpt-image-2/#nano-banana-2-and-pro) when I tried this back in April. It spelled Forest Festival wrong in two different ways though.",
